       The function iitteemm__uusseerrppttrr returns a pointer (possibly NNUULLLL).   It  does
       not set eerrrrnnoo.

       The sseett__iitteemm__uusseerrppttrr always returns EE__OOKK (success).

PPOORRTTAABBIILLIITTYY
       These  routines  emulate the System V menu library.  They were not sup‐
       ported on Version 7 or BSD versions.

       The user pointer is a void pointer.  We chose not to leave it as a char
       pointer for SVr4 compatibility.

